  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A sequence XXX is defined as:\n\n\nX1=0;X_1 = 0;X1​=0;\nX2=A;X_2 = A;X2​=A;\nX3=B;X_3 = B;X3​=B;\nXiX_iXi​ = Xi−1+Xi−2−Xi−3X_{i-1} + X_{i-2} - X_{i-3}Xi−1​+Xi−2​−Xi−3​ for all i&gt;3i &gt; 3i&gt;3.\nGiven an integer KKK, find the KthK^{th}Kth **smallest** element of sequence XXX.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three space-separated integers AAA, BBB, and KKK, as mentioned in the statement.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the KthK^{th}Kth smallest element in the sequence.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^{5}1≤T≤105",
      "1≤A,B,K≤1091 \\leq A, B, K \\leq 10^{9}1≤A,B,K≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
